Subject: gl: GLSL 1.20 texture lookups without a bias argument when the bias is 0

The 3D shaders (terrain, decals, models, buttons) sample through a macro that is texture2D(tex, uv,
bias) on GLSL 1.20, and the bias is WZ_MIP_LOAD_BIAS, 0 unless the config sets one. Mesa's nv30
compiles a biased lookup to the RSX's TXB, which samples wrong whatever the bias: on the PS3 the
whole 3D view was dark and flat while the UI (texture2D without bias) was right. A shader mod
drawing the same lookups as TEX and as TXB in stripes showed it (2026-10-20). When there is no bias
to apply, rewrite the macro to texture2D(tex, uv): the same lookup on every driver. Mesa patch 0045
fixes it on the driver side too; this keeps the game right with a Mesa without it.

---
diff --git a/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp b/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp
--- a/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp
+++ b/lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp
@@ -1148,6 +1148,18 @@
 			{
 				patchFragmentShaderTextureLodBias(fragmentShaderStr, mipLodBias.value());
 			}
+			if (!mipLodBias.has_value() || mipLodBias.value() == 0.f)
+			{
+				// GLSL 1.20 shaders sample through texture2D(tex, uv, bias); with no bias to apply,
+				// drop the argument: a plain lookup instead of one with a bias of 0 (Mesa's nv30 turns
+				// the biased one into the RSX's TXB, which samples wrong: the PS3's 3D view was dark)
+				const std::string biasMacro = "#define texture(tex,uv,bias) texture2D(tex,uv,bias)";
+				size_t pos = fragmentShaderStr.find(biasMacro);
+				if (pos != std::string::npos)
+				{
+					fragmentShaderStr.replace(pos, biasMacro.size(), "#define texture(tex,uv,bias) texture2D(tex,uv)");
+				}
+			}
 
 			const char* ShaderStrings[2] = { fragment_header, fragmentShaderStr.c_str() };
 
